# Git for Windows checks out with CRLF by default. The Gradle wrapper is a
# POSIX shell script — CRLF line endings make it fail to run on macOS, Linux
# and CI with a "bad interpreter" error. Pin it to LF on every platform.
gradlew text eol=lf

# ...and pin the Windows counterparts to CRLF for the same reason.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The Vosk speech model is 54 MB of binary that git currently leaves alone only
# because core.autocrlf happens to be false here. A clone with autocrlf=true, or
# anyone adding `* text=auto` later, would rewrite bytes inside .mdl/.fst files
# and the decoder would fail at runtime with nothing pointing back at git.
# Marked binary so that can't happen: no eol conversion, no diffing.
android/app/src/voice/assets/model-en/** binary
